With the core platform stable, the next layer is exchange: a marketplace that connects the people who make creative tools with the people who need them.

# Three ways to transact

Creator crowdfunding lets a community fund a project directly. Digital product distribution handles templates, plugins, courses, and technical documents with one-click licensing. Collaboration matching pairs complementary creators around a project brief, for a sprint or a longer partnership.

# Built on CreaSDK

The marketplace uses CreaSDK's payment and distribution modules, so licensing and settlement follow the same primitives as the rest of the platform. We are also exploring smart-contract revenue splits for multi-author projects, with transparent attribution and automatic payouts.

# The MVP

The first version opens to 50 creators from the core community in Q4. The goal is not catalogue size. It is to prove that a small, trusted market can settle payments and disputes better than a general-purpose platform.
